==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cooldown Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Bombercat''' when obtained from [[Bloomin' Brightly (Easy)|Bloomin' Brightly]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
Flower Cat and Cooldown Cat are practically as useless against [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] as against non-Dark enemies, due to their single-target attacks and low freeze chance. They can only be useful against [[Dark Cyclone]] and [[Razorback]], optimizing their low range.

==='''True Form'''===
In True Form, Bombercat easily becomes an anti-Dark mainstay, being able to shut down almost all Dark enemies either when stacked and protected, or with help from [[Cat Combo|Combos]]. By default, only 2 are needed to perma-freeze, allowing him to counter even the most dangerous and dense swarms of Dark enemies as they usually have just around 200 range or less. When used properly, he can reduce Dark-focused stages such as [[Tempered in Flame (Deadly)|XP Colosseum]], [[Revenge of D-Cyclone (Deadly)|Revenge of D-Cyclone]] and [[Taste of Success (Merciless)|Merciless XP]] to rubble. With maxed [[Void Fruit]] Treasures and a Freeze Up M Combo, Bomber reaches full uptime on its own, giving them no opportunity to break free unless they reposition. This is most notable against the likes of [[Le'Grim]] and [[Le'noir]], as just one Bomber can completely immobilize them if given a window of opportunity.

Bombercat is not without weaknesses, however, and they can become clear in later levels of [[Legend Stages]]. His long backswing renders him open to enemies' attacks, and when Bombercat misses, he will be unlikely to survive due to how aggressive Dark enemies can get. Longer-ranged Dark enemies like [[Director Kurosawah]] can also be a problem as he may perish before he can reach them. This can be a very serious problem for Bombercat, especially on stages which mix Dark threats with others ([[The Holy Exploit]], [[The Spy Who Pet Me]], [[Primitive Souls]], etc.) or if they are impossible to freeze due to other complications ([[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]]'s rapid attacks knocking Dark enemies away, [[Ragin' Gory]]'s freeze immunity, curse disabling his ability, etc). While in some cases, you can still let the next one take over, you will inevitably lose a lot of ground. The best thing you can do to fix this problem is to time your Bombercat well so he doesn't miss his target and freezes a large number of Dark enemies.

