==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Flower Cat was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Nostalgia (Removed Combo)|Nostalgia]] and [[Electric Home (Removed Combo)|Electric Home]].
*Cooldown Cat appears behind the door in the menu during the [[Summer Break Cats|Summer Break Cats event]].
*Flower Cat's design and attack animation reference the [[wikipedia:ja:フラワーロック|FLOWER ROCK]], a toy potted flower first released by Tomy in 1988. The toy would "[https://youtu.be/o4Cr5XRsI24 dance]" in response to sound such as clapping, just like in Flower Cat's attack animation. Flower Cat was in the [[Nostalgia (Removed Combo)|Nostalgia Combo]] because the FLOWER ROCK is an old toy.
*Bombercat is an obvious reference to the [[wikipedia:Bomberman|Bomberman]] franchise and its eponymous protagonist.
*In the [[The Battle Cats POP!|Nintendo 3DS version]], Flower Cat is a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] and can be unlocked via the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]].
*In The Nintendo Switch version, Bombercat is an unobtainable [[True Form]] that can only be accessible via save file editing.

